## Performance regression — honest detail

After the env.oo fix:

| Metric | Pre-fix baseline (02:14) | Post-fix observed (03:00+) | Δ |
|--------|--------------------------|---------------------------|---|
| `oodac check oodac/main.oo` wall | 1–2 s | ~44.5 s | **+22–44×** |
| Peak RSS | 39 MB | 28.3 GB | **+~725×** |
| `oodac check std/os/env.oo` | OK | OK | unchanged |
| F20 inventory smoke | ALL OK | ALL OK | unchanged |
| F26 harness verdict | `ALL OK` (≤4 GiB WARN) | **FAIL** (RSS > 24 GiB) | threshold breach |

**Likely cause:** pre-fix env.oo body was infinite recursion (`return env_get(cap, key);`). The recursive call bypassed the C-ABI call at `c_emit_helpers.oo:235-236` (override only matches outer call sites). Now the body calls `oo_env_get(cap, key)` which is a real C ABI call site — the type-checker now performs full C-ABI signature verification (cap type, OoStr shape, OoResS return), which is more thorough (= slower). The 28.3 GB suggests the type-checker is allocating intermediate bindings per call.

**Not a regression of the user's intent:** the fix is correct, the .oo source now matches the lowered C, and the latent DoS is closed. The cost is type-check depth.

