## Follow-up residual (NOT closed this turn)

- **B6 — HIGH: revert env.oo fix OR bound the type-checker.** Decision gate for the owner. Revert restores the 1–2s / 39 MB baseline but reintroduces the latent stack-overflow. Keep the fix and the type-checker cost is real. Either: (a) revert, (b) keep and tune the type-checker, (c) keep and document the cost.
- **B7 — MED: F26 harness threshold recalibration.** The 24 GiB WARN/FAIL gate was set when peak RSS was 22.8 GB. New peak is 28.3 GB. Either raise the threshold or flag the regression as a separate concern.
- **B8 — CRIT: trace the wall/RSS blow-up.** The 22× slowdown and 725× RSS growth is not in scope of this fix. Likely the type-checker is allocating per-call. Needs a profile.

